<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>P2P 60-24 EVO — GitHub Copilot Integration Guide</title>
    <style>
        * {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }
        body {
            font-family: 'Monaco', 'Courier New', monospace;
            background: #0f0f23;
            color: #e0e0e0;
            line-height: 1.6;
            padding: 2rem;
        }
        .container {
            max-width: 1200px;
            margin: 0 auto;
        }
        header {
            text-align: center;
            margin-bottom: 3rem;
            border-bottom: 2px solid #00d4ff;
            padding-bottom: 2rem;
        }
        header h1 {
            color: #00d4ff;
            font-size: 2rem;
            margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
        }
        header p {
            color: #aaa;
        }
        .section {
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
            border: 1px solid #00d4ff;
            border-radius: 8px;
            padding: 2rem;
            margin-bottom: 2rem;
            backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
        }
        .section h2 {
            color: #00d4ff;
            margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
            font-size: 1.5rem;
        }
        .prompt-box {
            background: #1a1a2e;
            border: 2px solid #ffa500;
            border-radius: 8px;
            padding: 1.5rem;
            margin: 1.5rem 0;
            position: relative;
        }
        .prompt-box h3 {
            color: #ffa500;
            margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
            font-size: 1rem;
        }
        .prompt-text {
            background: #0f0f23;
            border: 1px solid #00d4ff;
            padding: 1rem;
            border-radius: 4px;
            color: #00d4ff;
            white-space: pre-wrap;
            word-wrap: break-word;
            font-size: 0.9rem;
            line-height: 1.5;
            margin-bottom: 1rem;
        }
        .copy-btn {
            position: absolute;
            top: 1rem;
            right: 1rem;
            background: #00d4ff;
            color: #000;
            border: none;
            padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
            border-radius: 4px;
            cursor: pointer;
            font-weight: bold;
            font-size: 0.85rem;
        }
        .copy-btn:hover {
            background: #00ff00;
        }
        .instruction {
            background: rgba(0, 212, 255, 0.1);
            border-left: 3px solid #00d4ff;
            padding: 1rem;
            margin: 1rem 0;
            border-radius: 4px;
        }
        .warning {
            background: rgba(255, 165, 0, 0.1);
            border-left: 3px solid #ffa500;
            padding: 1rem;
            margin: 1rem 0;
            border-radius: 4px;
        }
        .success {
            background: rgba(0, 212, 0, 0.1);
            border-left: 3px solid #00d400;
            padding: 1rem;
            margin: 1rem 0;
            border-radius: 4px;
        }
        code {
            background: #1a1a2e;
            color: #00ff00;
            padding: 2px 6px;
            border-radius: 3px;
            font-size: 0.9rem;
        }
        .step {
            margin: 1.5rem 0;
            padding: 1rem;
            border-left: 4px solid #ffa500;
            background: rgba(255, 165, 0, 0.05);
        }
        .step.ready {
            border-left-color: #00d400;
            background: rgba(0, 212, 0, 0.05);
        }
        .step h3 {
            color: #ffa500;
            margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
        }
        .step.ready h3 {
            color: #00d400;
        }
        ul {
            margin: 1rem 0 1rem 2rem;
        }
        li {
            margin: 0.5rem 0;
        }
        .footer {
            text-align: center;
            color: #666;
            padding-top: 2rem;
            border-top: 1px solid rgba(0, 212, 255, 0.3);
            margin-top: 3rem;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <header>
            <h1>🤖 GitHub Copilot Integration — P2P 60-24 EVO</h1>
            <p>Prompts for Phase 1 implementation in VS Code</p>
            <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; margin-top: 0.5rem; color: #666;">Session 3 | Ready for Team Execution</p>
        </header>

        <!-- SETUP SECTION -->
        <div class="section">
            <h2>📋 Setup: Copilot in VS Code</h2>

            <div class="instruction">
                <strong>Prerequisites:</strong>
                <ul>
                    <li>VS Code installed</li>
                    <li>GitHub Copilot extension (free trial or subscription)</li>
                    <li>Logged in to GitHub</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="step ready">
                <h3>✅ Step 1: Install Copilot</h3>
                <p>In VS Code:</p>
                <ol>
                    <li>Extensions → search "GitHub Copilot"</li>
                    <li>Install official extension by GitHub</li>
                    <li>Sign in with GitHub account</li>
                    <li>Enable Copilot Chat (alternative: <code>Ctrl+Shift+I</code>)</li>
                </ol>
            </div>

            <div class="step ready">
                <h3>✅ Step 2: Clone Repository</h3>
                <div class="prompt-text">git clone https://github.com/P2P-60-24/p2p-60-24-evo.git
cd p2p-60-24-evo
code .</div>
            </div>

            <div class="step ready">
                <h3>✅ Step 3: Open Copilot Chat</h3>
                <p>In VS Code: <code>Ctrl+Shift+I</code> (Windows/Linux) or <code>Cmd+Shift+I</code> (Mac)</p>
                <p>Then paste any prompt below</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- IDENTITY MODULE PROMPTS -->
        <div class="section">
            <h2>🔐 Module 1: Identity (ADR-001)</h2>

            <div class="prompt-box">
                <h3>Prompt A: Implement Ed25519 Signing Tests</h3>
                <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this)">Copy</button>
                <div class="prompt-text">Write comprehensive unit tests for pkg/identity/identity.go
Tests should verify:
1. New() generates valid Ed25519 keypair
2. Sign() produces valid 64-byte signature
3. Verify() correctly validates signatures
4. Invalid signatures are rejected
5. Edge cases: nil inputs, empty messages

Follow Go testing conventions. Use testify/assert.
Target: >90% coverage</div>
            </div>

            <div class="prompt-box">
                <h3>Prompt B: Add Identity Serialization</h3>
                <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this)">Copy</button>
                <div class="prompt-text">Extend pkg/identity/identity.go with serialization:

Add methods:
- MarshalJSON() → JSON representation (public key only)
- UnmarshalJSON() → restore from JSON
- Serialize() → bytes representation for transport
- Deserialize(data []byte) → restore from bytes

Ensure private key is NEVER serialized.
Add error handling for malformed inputs.
Include unit tests.</div>
            </div>

            <div class="prompt-box">
                <h3>Prompt C: Multi-Key Identity Management</h3>
                <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this)">Copy</button>
                <div class="prompt-text">Create pkg/identity/manager.go:

IdentityManager should:
- Store multiple identities (map[string]*Identity)
- Generate new identities on demand
- Load/save identities from persistent storage
- List all managed identities
- Rotate primary identity

Methods:
- CreateIdentity(name string) (*Identity, error)
- GetIdentity(nodeID string) (*Identity, bool)
- ListIdentities() []string
- DeleteIdentity(nodeID string) error

Thread-safe with sync.RWMutex</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- TRANSPORT MODULE PROMPTS -->
        <div class="section">
            <h2>📡 Module 2: Transport (ADR-002)</h2>

            <div class="prompt-box">
                <h3>Prompt A: Implement UDP Message Serialization</h3>
                <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this)">Copy</button>
                <div class="prompt-text">Extend pkg/transport/transport.go Message struct:

Add serialization:
- Message.Marshal() → []byte (MessagePack or JSON)
- UnmarshalMessage(data []byte) → *Message
- Encrypt payload with sender's Ed25519 public key
- Add version field for backward compatibility

Test with various payload sizes (0 bytes to 4KB)
Ensure signature verification works
Include fuzzing tests</div>
            </div>

            <div class="prompt-box">
                <h3>Prompt B: Complete UDP Listen Loop</h3>
                <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this)">Copy</button>
                <div class="prompt-text">Implement UDP6024.listen() method:

1. Deserialize incoming UDP packets
2. Verify Ed25519 signature from sender
3. Call all registered handlers
4. Handle errors gracefully (malformed packets)
5. Measure latency of handler execution
6. Add debug logging for packet flow

Add metrics:
- packets_received
- packets_dropped
- handler_errors

Thread-safe channel for shutdown signal</div>
            </div>

            <div class="prompt-box">
                <h3>Prompt C: Peer Discovery & Registry</h3>
                <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this)">Copy</button>
                <div class="prompt-text">Create pkg/transport/peerdiscovery.go:

PeerRegistry should:
- Track known peers (NodeID → UDPAddr)
- Auto-expire stale peers (30 min TTL)
- Support mDNS discovery (optional)
- Periodic ping to check liveness
- Exponential backoff retry

Methods:
- RegisterPeer(nodeID, addr string)
- GetPeer(nodeID string) (*net.UDPAddr, error)
- GetActivePeers() []string
- RemovePeer(nodeID string)

Add tests for TTL expiration</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- EVENTBUS MODULE PROMPTS -->
        <div class="section">
            <h2>📊 Module 3: EventBus</h2>

            <div class="prompt-box">
                <h3>Prompt A: Event Serialization & Persistence</h3>
                <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this)">Copy</button>
                <div class="prompt-text">Extend pkg/eventbus/eventbus.go:

Add persistence layer:
- SaveEvent(evt *Event) error → write to file/DB
- LoadEvents(since time.Time) []*Event
- Checkpoint() []byte → snapshot for recovery
- Replay([]byte) error → restore from snapshot

Implement 30-day retention:
- Auto-cleanup old events (cron job)
- Batch deletes for performance

Use JSON format for events.
Add compression for archived events.
Include tests for recovery scenarios</div>
            </div>

            <div class="prompt-box">
                <h3>Prompt B: 2-of-3 Quorum Validation</h3>
                <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this)">Copy</button>
                <div class="prompt-text">Implement quorum verification in EventBus:

Add QuorumValidator:
- Track 3 validator nodes (hardcoded or config)
- Require 2-of-3 signatures on critical events
- Events types requiring quorum:
  * EVENT_STATE_UPDATED
  * EVENT_GROUP_FORMED
  * EVENT_REPUTATION_UPDATED

Methods:
- RequiresQuorum(eventType EventType) bool
- ValidateQuorum(evt *Event, sigs [][]byte) bool
- AddSignature(evt *Event, sig []byte) error

Test: fail if <2 signatures, pass if ≥2</div>
            </div>

            <div class="prompt-box">
                <h3>Prompt C: Event Replay & Recovery</h3>
                <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this)">Copy</button>
                <div class="prompt-text">Create pkg/eventbus/recovery.go:

EventRecoveryManager should:
- Load event log from disk on startup
- Replay events in chronological order
- Rebuild state from events (event sourcing)
- Detect gaps/missing events
- Validate event chain integrity

Recovery flow:
1. Load checkpoint
2. Replay events since checkpoint
3. Validate final state hash
4. Report recovery status

Add metrics:
- events_replayed
- recovery_time_ms
- final_state_hash

Include integration tests</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- STATESTORE MODULE PROMPTS -->
        <div class="section">
            <h2>💾 Module 4: StateStore (BadgerDB)</h2>

            <div class="prompt-box">
                <h3>Prompt A: BadgerDB Integration</h3>
                <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this)">Copy</button>
                <div class="prompt-text">Implement BadgerDB backend in pkg/statestore/statestore.go:

Extend BadgerStore:
- Initialize BadgerDB with default config
- Implement Put() with LWW CRDT semantics
- Implement Get(), Delete(), Range()
- Handle DB corruption gracefully
- Support snapshots (backup/restore)

Add:
- Compaction strategy (weekly)
- GC settings (70% DISCARD_RATIO)
- Key versioning (metadata tracking)

Include tests:
- Concurrent put/get operations
- LWW conflict resolution
- Recovery from corruption</div>
            </div>

            <div class="prompt-box">
                <h3>Prompt B: CRDT Merge & Conflict Resolution</h3>
                <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this)">Copy</button>
                <div class="prompt-text">Create pkg/statestore/crdt.go:

LWWRegister (Last-Write-Wins):
- Timestamp-based conflict resolution
- Bias toward higher timestamp
- Handle clock skew (3s tolerance)

Methods:
- Merge(local, remote StateEntry) StateEntry
- ResolveConflict(entries []StateEntry) StateEntry

Multi-value CRDT (optional):
- Keep version history
- Track causality with vector clocks
- Support application-level conflict resolution

Add comprehensive tests:
- Concurrent updates
- Network delays
- Clock inconsistencies</div>
            </div>

            <div class="prompt-box">
                <h3>Prompt C: Snapshot & Restore</h3>
                <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this)">Copy</button>
                <div class="prompt-text">Implement snapshot management in StateStore:

Add methods:
- Snapshot() ([]byte, error) → complete state dump
- Restore([]byte) error → load from snapshot
- IncrementalSnapshot() → delta since last
- VerifyChecksum() error → validate snapshot integrity

Snapshot format:
- Version header
- Timestamp
- All KV pairs with timestamps
- SHA256 checksum

Use gzip compression.
Incremental snapshots track last change timestamp.
Include background snapshot task (hourly).</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- MATCHING MODULE PROMPTS -->
        <div class="section">
            <h2>🎯 Module 5: MatchingOrchestrator</h2>

            <div class="prompt-box">
                <h3>Prompt A: Implement Matching Algorithm</h3>
                <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this)">Copy</button>
                <div class="prompt-text">Improve pkg/matching/orchestrator.go matching logic:

Current algorithm is greedy. Enhance with:
1. Scoring function:
   - Quality factor (0-1)
   - Quantity ratio (normalized)
   - Buyer/seller reputation (0-1)
   - Composite score = 0.4*quality + 0.4*quantity + 0.2*reputation

2. Ranking:
   - Sort matches by score (descending)
   - Return top N matches (default 5)

3. Edge cases:
   - Partial fulfillment (buyer accepts 80%)
   - Multiple sellers for one need
   - Bidding/negotiation

Add unit tests with sample data.</div>
            </div>

            <div class="prompt-box">
                <h3>Prompt B: Match Lifecycle & State Transitions</h3>
                <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this)">Copy</button>
                <div class="prompt-text">Create pkg/matching/lifecycle.go:

MatchState enum:
- PROPOSED (initial match)
- NEGOTIATING (parties discussing)
- ACCEPTED (both agreed)
- REJECTED (one party declined)
- COMPLETED (fulfilled)
- DISPUTED (conflict)
- ARCHIVED (closed)

MatchLifecycle:
- TransitionTo(state MatchState) error
- ValidateTransition(from, to) bool
- OnStateChange(handler func)
- RollbackIfFailed()

Add state machine validation:
- PROPOSED → NEGOTIATING, REJECTED
- NEGOTIATING → ACCEPTED, REJECTED
- ACCEPTED → COMPLETED, DISPUTED
- etc.

Include timeout handling (30 day max).</div>
            </div>

            <div class="prompt-box">
                <h3>Prompt C: Persistent Match Storage</h3>
                <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this)">Copy</button>
                <div class="prompt-text">Extend MatchingOrchestrator with persistence:

Save/load matches to StateStore:
- Key: "matches:{matchID}"
- Value: serialized Match + Lifecycle

Methods:
- SaveMatch(m *Match) error
- LoadMatch(matchID string) (*Match, error)
- LoadMatchesByNeed(needID string) []*Match
- LoadMatchesBySeller(sellerID string) []*Match

Query methods:
- GetActive() []*Match (exclude COMPLETED/ARCHIVED)
- GetExpired() []*Match (>30 days)
- GetByState(state MatchState) []*Match

Add background cleanup task.</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- REPUTATION MODULE PROMPTS -->
        <div class="section">
            <h2>⭐ Module 6: ReputationWeighter</h2>

            <div class="prompt-box">
                <h3>Prompt A: Bayesian Update Optimization</h3>
                <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this)">Copy</button>
                <div class="prompt-text">Optimize Bayesian updates in pkg/reputation/weighter.go:

Current: simple alpha/beta increment.

Enhance:
1. Weighted feedback:
   - RecordSuccess(nodeID, weight float64) → alpha += weight
   - weight based on match value, recency
   - recent interactions weighted 2x more

2. Feedback quality:
   - Verified feedback (2.0x multiplier)
   - Contested feedback (0.5x multiplier, disputed)
   - Unverified feedback (1.0x baseline)

3. Convergence tracking:
   - Calculate confidence interval (95%)
   - Return bool when confident (narrow CI)
   - High variance early → narrow over time

Add tests with various alpha/beta ratios.</div>
            </div>

            <div class="prompt-box">
                <h3>Prompt B: Decay Algorithm Implementation</h3>
                <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this)">Copy</button>
                <div class="prompt-text">Enhance ApplyDecay() in ReputationRecord:

Current: 0.99/week multiplier.

Improve:
1. Recency bias:
   - Recent interactions decay slower
   - Older interactions decay faster
   - Half-life = 30 days for neutral score

2. Tier protection:
   - EXEMPLARY (>0.8): decay 0.98/week
   - VERIFIED (0.6-0.8): decay 0.99/week
   - TRUSTED (0.4-0.6): decay 0.995/week
   - NOVICE (<0.4): decay 1.0/week (no decay)

3. Persistence:
   - Save decay progress to StateStore
   - Resume from last checkpoint on restart

Add unit tests with time advancement.</div>
            </div>

            <div class="prompt-box">
                <h3>Prompt C: Reputation Analytics & Metrics</h3>
                <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this)">Copy</button>
                <div class="prompt-text">Create pkg/reputation/analytics.go:

ReputationAnalytics:
- GetDistribution() → histogram of scores (10 buckets)
- GetTierCounts() → {TIER: count}
- GetTrustNetwork() → nodes with score > 0.5
- GetOutliers() → nodes with unusual patterns

Metrics:
- average_reputation (network-wide)
- reputation_variance
- tier_distribution
- recent_change_rate (how fast scores changing)

Methods:
- Forecast(nodeID, days int) float64 → predict future score
- GetInfluencers() []string → high-reputation nodes
- GetRiskNodes() []string → declining reputation

Export as JSON/CSV for analysis.</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- GROUP & CONTEXT PROMPTS -->
        <div class="section">
            <h2>👥 Modules 7-8: GroupManager & ContextManager</h2>

            <div class="prompt-box">
                <h3>Prompt A: Dunbar Circle Implementation</h3>
                <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this)">Copy</button>
                <div class="prompt-text">Extend pkg/group/group.go with Dunbar mechanics:

Current: basic member tracking.

Add:
1. Dynamic rebalancing:
   - DUNBAR_INNERMOST (5): highest trust
   - DUNBAR_INNER (15): close ties
   - DUNBAR_MIDDLE (50): friends
   - DUNBAR_OUTER (150): acquaintances
   - Automatically move members between circles based on interaction

2. Activity scoring:
   - Interactions increase trust within circle
   - Inactivity triggers demotion
   - Betrayal triggers expulsion

3. Circle eviction policy:
   - When full, demote least-trusted member
   - Provide grace period before removal

Add tests: member lifecycle, circle transitions.</div>
            </div>

            <div class="prompt-box">
                <h3>Prompt B: Context Boundaries & Access Control</h3>
                <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this)">Copy</button>
                <div class="prompt-text">Enhance pkg/context/context.go:

Add access control:
1. Roles in context:
   - OWNER (creator, full control)
   - MEMBER (can read, propose actions)
   - OBSERVER (read-only)
   - BANNED (no access)

2. Permissions:
   - AddParticipant(nodeID, role) error
   - CanRead(nodeID) bool
   - CanWrite(nodeID) bool
   - CanModerate(nodeID) bool

3. Context quotas:
   - Max participants per context
   - Storage limit for context data
   - Time limits (expire after TTL)

4. Audit log:
   - Track who changed what when
   - Immutable event log

Add tests: permission matrix, role transitions.</div>
            </div>

            <div class="prompt-box">
                <h3>Prompt C: Group & Context Persistence</h3>
                <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this)">Copy</button>
                <div class="prompt-text">Implement persistence for Groups & Contexts:

Save to StateStore:
- Key: "groups:{groupID}" or "contexts:{contextID}"
- Value: serialized struct + metadata

Add methods:
- (gm *GroupManager) SaveAll() error
- (gm *GroupManager) LoadAll() error
- (cm *ContextManager) SaveAll() error
- (cm *ContextManager) LoadAll() error

Consistency:
- Atomic writes (all or nothing)
- Versioning (detect conflicts)
- Snapshot on every change

Recovery:
- Load on startup
- Verify integrity
- Replay pending actions

Add tests: crash recovery, concurrent access.</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- TESTING PROMPTS -->
        <div class="section">
            <h2>🧪 Testing & Quality</h2>

            <div class="prompt-box">
                <h3>Prompt A: Integration Tests</h3>
                <button class="copy-btn" onclick="copyPrompt(this)">Copy</button>
                <div class="prompt-text">Create pkg/integration_test.go:

End-to-end test scenarios:
1. Two-node exchange:
   - Node A publishes NEED for resource X
   - Node B publishes OFFER for resource X
   - EventBus notifies both
   - MatchingOrchestrator finds match
   - Both reputation scores updated
   - Context created for transaction

2. Network resilience:
   - Drop packet, retry succeeds
   - Replay duplicate message (idempotent)
   - Concurrent updates to same state

3. Complete lifecycle:
   - Node startup
   - Identity generation
   - Transport initialization
   - EventBus subscription
   - Publish Need/Offer
   - Match found
   - Reputation updated
   - Graceful shutdown

Run with: go test -v -run TestIntegration ./...